Hi Mario/Jim,

Thank you for sharing your thoughts on this.

Let me remind that the reasoning for having such policy in the charter is to =
ensure that we are defining new mappings that are motivated by real operation=
al needs.

Process-wise, consensus to adopt a document does not mean that the document w=
ill be necessary progressed to an RFC. Consensus to publish will typically be=
 assessed during WGLC. Also, a WG may decide to adopt a doc, but decide later=
 that it is better to park a spec , etc.

Now back to this specific document, the information you shared below is a gre=
at info to record in the document writeup to demonstrate how it adheres to th=
e deployment policy in the charter.

FYI, we received comments during the IESG review of the QUIC draft on that sa=
me point. We managed to address it as I already had the required arguments ga=
thered as part of my AD review (thanks to the authors).

Thank you.

Cheers,
Med

De : Mario Loffredo <mario.loffredo@iit.cnr.it>
